---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import Sprig from '../components/Sprig.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Radiant Gardens runs on a Master Craftsman model: the founder personally designs, builds, and supports every food garden in the Finger Lakes region. Meet the philosophy behind the work."
>
  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>A craftsman's approach to food gardens</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Radiant Gardens runs on a simple, old-fashioned idea: the person who
        designs your garden should be the person who builds it — and who stands
        behind it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-paper">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="service-detail">
        <div class="sticky-label">
          <Sprig />
          <p class="eyebrow">The founder</p>
          <h2>Built by one pair of hands</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>
            The founder of Radiant Gardens comes to garden-making from systems
            engineering — a career of designing things that work reliably —
            joined with a long-held passion for sustainable agriculture. It
            turns out a kitchen garden is a system too: sun, soil, water, and
            seasons, arranged so that food simply follows.
          </p>
          <p>
            Radiant Gardens works on a "Master Craftsman" model. There are no
            crews and no hand-offs: the founder personally designs and builds
            every garden, then personally supports it for as long as you grow.
            The number of gardens built each year is deliberately small, so every
            project gets full attention — and every client gets the artisan, not
            a rotating crew.
          </p>
          <p>
            When Radiant Gardens launches in 2026, that's the experience you can
            expect: one expert, from first sketch to first harvest.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">What we value</p>
        <h2>Four commitments behind every garden</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid cols-2">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon"><Icon name="trowel" /></div>
          <h3>Craftsmanship</h3>
          <p>
            Every garden is a signature piece — built from quality materials,
            set level, and finished with care we'd want in our own yard.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon"><Icon name="sprout" /></div>
          <h3>Empowerment</h3>
          <p>
            A garden should succeed under your hands, not ours. We teach, coach,
            and equip you to grow with confidence.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon"><Icon name="leafy" /></div>
          <h3>Sustainability</h3>
          <p>
            In the materials we choose, the way we build, and the way we run the
            business — a garden should give back more than it takes.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon"><Icon name="hub" /></div>
          <h3>Partnership</h3>
          <p>
            We're in it for the long haul. Every garden includes lifetime
            support, because a garden is never really "finished."
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container center">
      <div class="divider" role="presentation"><Sprig /></div>
      <h2>Where we work</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-inline: auto">
        Radiant Gardens serves families across the Finger Lakes region of
        Upstate New York — including Ithaca, Corning, Horseheads, Elmira, and
        the surrounding communities.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="container">
      <Sprig />
      <h2>Grow with us</h2>
      <p>
        We're preparing for our first season in 2026. If a founder-built food
        garden sounds like your kind of project, we'd love to meet you.
      </p>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Say hello</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
